<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/3rd-century-bce">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of the Great Plains</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/203-bce">203 BCE</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century-bce">3rd century BCE</a> · Also known as Battle of Campi Magni · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-punic-war">Second Punic War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of the Great Plains was fought in 203 BCE in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/medjerda">Bagradas</a> valley of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-africa">North Africa</a>, in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tunisia">Tunisia</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scipio-africanus">Scipio Africanus</a> defeated a Carthaginian and Numidian army under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hasdrubal-gisco">Hasdrubal Gisco</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syphax">Syphax</a>, which included about 4,000 Celtiberian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mercenary">mercenaries</a> who fought to the last. The defeat led <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carthage">Carthage</a> to recall <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hannibal">Hannibal</a> from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-the-great-plains.jpg" alt="Battle of the Great Plains" width="320" height="480" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: José Luiz · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bust_of_Sulla_(loan_from_Ny_Carlsberg_Glyptotek)_-_Glyptothek_-_Munich_-_Germany_2017.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
